\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There is a land of pure delight,
\par Where saint immortal reign;
\par Infinite day excludes the night,
\par And pleasures banish pain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There everlasting spring abides,
\par And never- withering flowers;
\par Death, like a narrow sea, divides
\par This heavenly land from ours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Sweet fields beyond the swelling
\par flood
\par Stand dressed in living green;
\par So to the Jews old  Canaan stood,
\par While Jordan rolled between.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. But timorous mortals start and shrink
\par To cross this narrow sea,
\par And linger, shivering on the brink,
\par And fear to launch away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O could we make our doubts remove,
\par Those gloomy thoughts that rise,
\par And see the Canaan that we love 
\par With unbeclouded eyes:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Could we but climb where Moses stood,
\par And view the landscape o'er,
\par Not Jordan's stream, nor death's 
\par cold flood,
\par Should fright us from the shore!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

